WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.049 --> 00:00:04.470
Film Courage: When that person said to you
“Hollywood will only make you more of what

00:00:04.470 --> 00:00:07.120
you are,” what did you think in that moment?

00:00:07.120 --> 00:00:08.700
This was 10 years ago?

00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:12.420
John Paul Rice, Producer: No…18…19 years
ago?

00:00:12.420 --> 00:00:24.099
Um I got a little scared because I didn’t
know what does he see in me and I knew that

00:00:24.099 --> 00:00:30.769
I had certain family issues when I grew up
that’s kind of what got me into art (if

00:00:30.769 --> 00:00:35.040
I can say it), creative role.

00:00:35.040 --> 00:00:43.210
But I think also he was genuinely concerned
because he saw a decent person who had an

00:00:43.210 --> 00:00:48.449
idealistic view and there is nothing wrong
with that.

00:00:48.449 --> 00:00:56.050
But at the same time I think when you are
younger is just a position of not stupidity

00:00:56.050 --> 00:01:00.800
or foolishness or maybe just ignorance because
you don’t have that experience yet to know

00:01:00.800 --> 00:01:09.010
when you are tempted with something that you…if
you had your parent there it certainly wouldn’t

00:01:09.010 --> 00:01:11.640
be happening.

00:01:11.640 --> 00:01:13.810
You wouldn’t be contemplating well maybe
I should.

00:01:13.810 --> 00:01:20.900
But in the moment you don’t realize that
when you are open and you’re sensitive,

00:01:20.900 --> 00:01:23.530
some of that can come from trauma.

00:01:23.530 --> 00:01:29.130
And you don’t realize that your reality
as you see it in front of you is actually

00:01:29.130 --> 00:01:30.890
a reflection of that.

00:01:30.890 --> 00:01:38.430
So every choice you make seems reasonable
but it may be coming from a place of fear,

00:01:38.430 --> 00:01:45.561
it may be coming from a place of reaction
where you had to do something (this is some

00:01:45.561 --> 00:01:49.220
of the stuff I’ve learned) where people
who are criminals (I’m just taking this

00:01:49.220 --> 00:01:53.680
as an extreme), we see high-speed car chases
all the time, right?

00:01:53.680 --> 00:01:58.800
We all know how that ends for the last 20
years, we see that when the car chase ends

00:01:58.800 --> 00:02:02.390
when the cops are following you, you don’t
get away.

00:02:02.390 --> 00:02:07.240
But time and time again people continue to
do that.

00:02:07.240 --> 00:02:13.590
Reason being that I’ve learned in my research
and my own discovery (not that I’m a criminal)

00:02:13.590 --> 00:02:23.950
but a lot of what we do that is irrational
to the outside is in fact rational to us because

00:02:23.950 --> 00:02:30.950
it’s a positive behavior that warded off
something else that has been imprinted in

00:02:30.950 --> 00:02:37.131
us that this is what gives us a positive outcome
totally unconscious of it, totally about a

00:02:37.131 --> 00:02:38.890
set of choices.

00:02:38.890 --> 00:02:42.950
You wake up every day and you have a set of
choices and this person over here has a different

00:02:42.950 --> 00:02:54.660
set of choices and when he said that (I didn’t
understand the depth of it) but coming full

00:02:54.660 --> 00:02:58.316
circle now I would give that same advice to
any young person now, I would give that same

00:02:58.316 --> 00:03:00.459
advice now to any young person who is coming
out to LA.

00:03:00.459 --> 00:03:04.990
Not as a caution about them but to be mindful
of yourself.

00:03:04.990 --> 00:03:11.440
And watch how you respond, how you think,
how you act according with what is presented

00:03:11.440 --> 00:03:16.620
in front of you.

00:03:16.620 --> 00:03:23.990
And that sometimes takes some experience of
some very difficult decisions that you make

00:03:23.990 --> 00:03:36.650
that at the time seemed right or maybe not
so bad but as it played out you realized “Wow

00:03:36.650 --> 00:03:39.460
I really did screw up there.”

00:03:39.460 --> 00:03:43.390
Or “I made a bad choice and I went against
my gut instinct.”

00:03:43.390 --> 00:03:49.650
And I think that’s the best…I will say
this to anyone who is listening, your gut

00:03:49.650 --> 00:03:51.330
instinct is probably your best choice.

00:03:51.330 --> 00:03:58.660
The first thing that you think about in reaction
without knowing any information is probably

00:03:58.660 --> 00:04:06.440
the most honest of anything as opposed to
logically talk your way through it.

00:04:06.440 --> 00:04:12.900
I’ve had situations where I wanted certain
people do be part of our project and didn’t

00:04:12.900 --> 00:04:17.569
realize that they didn’t want to be a part
of our project, they needed a paycheck.

00:04:17.569 --> 00:04:25.280
Fine…that’s their right but because I
felt that I needed them I limited my choices

00:04:25.280 --> 00:04:32.710
to that individual and attached myself to
the idea that I had to make that work as opposed

00:04:32.710 --> 00:04:37.120
to opening up and looking at all the other
possibilities that are out there.

00:04:37.120 --> 00:04:44.889
Now that sounds very rational and logical
but at the time it was personal, it was emotional

00:04:44.889 --> 00:04:52.580
and I was attached to needing to have that
person validate what I was doing and win to

00:04:52.580 --> 00:04:53.580
get it.

00:04:53.580 --> 00:04:54.629
That’s my own personal issue.

00:04:54.629 --> 00:04:59.530
But if I’m not exploring that and looking
at the consequences of that thinking and that

00:04:59.530 --> 00:05:04.499
behavior and the outcomes that it gives me
then I only have one or two choices.

00:05:04.499 --> 00:05:10.009
I’m going to be completely stubborn and
I’m going to force it.

00:05:10.009 --> 00:05:17.509
Or all of the time and energy that I’m using
to look open and outward and look at other

00:05:17.509 --> 00:05:21.889
people who may be able to use that may be
able to give me what I want, that they truly

00:05:21.889 --> 00:05:28.949
want to find and find the best match and experience
has taught me that’s the best thing to do.

00:05:28.949 --> 00:05:33.219
Film Courage: It’s not just falling prey
to temptation.

00:05:33.219 --> 00:05:37.310
I know I’ve heard that recovery meeting
conventions are held in Las Vegas because

00:05:37.310 --> 00:05:44.610
what better place to test your sobriety and
every trigger you have would be Las Vegas.

00:05:44.610 --> 00:05:45.610
John: Trauma bonding!

00:05:45.610 --> 00:05:48.660
Film Courage: Yes, but flattery.

00:05:48.660 --> 00:05:53.590
And that’s something that as a young person,
you walk down the street and you get someone

00:05:53.590 --> 00:05:57.229
stopping your car and saying “You would
be perfect for this…”

00:05:57.229 --> 00:06:02.029
And especially to if you’re coming with
(let’s get really “therapist-y”) tools

00:06:02.029 --> 00:06:08.069
that are maybe the best, that is going to
be…you are going to hear angels singing.

00:06:08.069 --> 00:06:14.479
So if you see this enough you would be prey
to other things as well so I think flattery

00:06:14.479 --> 00:06:15.479
can [be dangerous].

00:06:15.479 --> 00:06:19.729
And it can happen later on and you’ll never
realize that you may never hear from that

00:06:19.729 --> 00:06:23.000
person again and that’s something you have
to guard yourself against.

00:06:23.000 --> 00:06:25.530
John: Yes, that’s an experience that I’ve
found.

00:06:25.530 --> 00:06:31.590
I’ve had people sit down with me full tilt
with meetings, having watch their previous

00:06:31.590 --> 00:06:36.860
films, having read their previous scripts
and offering a ton of things and I’m like

00:06:36.860 --> 00:06:39.460
“This sounds great!”

00:06:39.460 --> 00:06:44.210
And then nothing and “Oh I’m going to
introduce you to this person, that person.”

00:06:44.210 --> 00:06:51.720
You know, I don’t know what that person’s
motivations were or not but to spend my time

00:06:51.720 --> 00:07:00.370
getting upset about it or obsessing over it
or trying to figure out that person’s problem.

00:07:00.370 --> 00:07:10.039
I guess it only hurts me in the end but I’ve
encountered that before early on in my career

00:07:10.039 --> 00:07:12.169
as an actor in fact.

00:07:12.169 --> 00:07:18.059
Film Courage: Yes, they exist!

00:07:18.059 --> 00:07:24.319
John: You know…going out on a business meeting
and having things…we’re talking about

00:07:24.319 --> 00:07:28.439
an era of Me Too, it happens to guys too and
it’s not being talked about.

00:07:28.439 --> 00:07:29.439
Film Courage: Sure.

00:07:29.439 --> 00:07:34.939
John: But there are people in Hollywood and
they have a right to do what they want but

00:07:34.939 --> 00:07:43.639
when they cross the line you are not able
to conduct yourself as a person.

00:07:43.639 --> 00:07:47.160
You have to sort of adjust according to them.

00:07:47.160 --> 00:07:53.990
Now you are selling yourself into something
that is not really about you anymore.

00:07:53.990 --> 00:07:56.979
It’s about what you do for that person.

00:07:56.979 --> 00:08:03.310
And compliments are very easy to give.

00:08:03.310 --> 00:08:09.189
But at the same time you have to have your
own center (your own self-worth) so that you

00:08:09.189 --> 00:08:13.779
know that if you are dealing in business,
and you are talented, you believe in your

00:08:13.779 --> 00:08:19.800
talent, or you have something to offer, find
someone who is looking for that.

00:08:19.800 --> 00:08:23.309
The look and everything…I mean I do cast
all of our films.

00:08:23.309 --> 00:08:29.330
I have seen random people and have gone up
to them and said “You have a great presence.

00:08:29.330 --> 00:08:31.919
I’d really like to see what you look like
on camera.”

00:08:31.919 --> 00:08:35.589
And I mean that truthfully because I love
discoveries of talent, that’s how we’ve

00:08:35.589 --> 00:08:40.950
been able to make all of our movies with these
talented people who are not Union (most of

00:08:40.950 --> 00:08:43.319
them are not).

00:08:43.319 --> 00:08:46.750
And not because I’m against the Union but
just because of the cost and everything else

00:08:46.750 --> 00:08:54.680
that we are trying to do and pay everybody
but it has more to do with being authentic

00:08:54.680 --> 00:08:58.370
and being genuine and being professional.

00:08:58.370 --> 00:09:03.639
And I think you can be all of those things
and still get the desired result that you

00:09:03.639 --> 00:09:08.680
want without having to do all this other kind
of stuff which is more of like like “I’m

00:09:08.680 --> 00:09:13.170
going to make you feel good” so I can get
something from you.

00:09:13.170 --> 00:09:18.060
Which is all I have to offer you is the truth
according to what I see and I could be totally

00:09:18.060 --> 00:09:19.060
wrong.

00:09:19.060 --> 00:09:20.540
And you tell me “Hey, go ahead with yourself.

00:09:20.540 --> 00:09:21.540
Get lost.”

00:09:21.540 --> 00:09:23.210
But that’s your right.

00:09:23.210 --> 00:09:28.769
All I am trying to do is say “I see something
here.

00:09:28.769 --> 00:09:32.040
I think there is something really good here.

00:09:32.040 --> 00:09:35.350
And I’d like to see if it would work for
what I’d like to do.”

